ime of 42.950 was the fastest ever recorded for a 250 metre track. As expected, the final matched the two long-time rivals. Britain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/106890"} "Jamie Staff"] " started out the final by pulling ahead of " [:a {:href "/athletes/113167"} "Gregory Bauge"] " on the first lap. Kenny then took over and increased the lead slightly against " [:a {:href "/athletes/113168"} "Kevin Sireau"] ". The final lap matched long-time rivals Hoy and " [:a {:href "/athletes/90378"} "Arnaud Tournant"] ". But Hoy was virtually unstoppable in Beijing and Tournant lost even more ground, Britain winning the gold medal by 0.523 seconds, a large margin for the team sprint. By comparison, in the bronze medal match, Germany edged Australia by only 8/1000th’s of a second. Hoy would go on to win all three track sprint gold medals on the track in Beijing – sprint, keirin, and team sprint."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Great Britain"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "42,950 (1 h6)"] [:td {} "43.034 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "43.128 (1 h1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "11"} [:a {:href "/athletes/90388"} "Chris Hoy"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/113166"} "Jason Kenny"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/106890"} "Jamie Staff"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "France"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} "43,541 (1 h7)"] [:td {} "43.656 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "43.651 (2 h1)"] [:td